      {
        "id": 125333,
        "name": "Koga",
        "username": "Koga",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koga/{size}/2058_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-06T19:46:03.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Guise the Indisciminate Mindbreaker Living Weapon Seeker</p><p>Besides increasing his base power by 2 he also Increased damage by 1, first time each turn you're dealt damage, deal&nbsp;each target 1 damage, and whenever you deal damage you increase the next damage dealt to that target by 2. So whenever I was hit I'd then hit everyone for 2, and then increase the next damage they&nbsp;take by 2. Nearly killed us all with that combo. Some titles can combine into very nasty combos.</p><p>Love the Reckless title, makes me feel even better about giving my own custom hero that same ability long ago, even better when you double up on it. It took me many tries changing the ability to finally settle on how it would work. Just like when I saw The Sentinels, I'd been working on my own multi character hero but in that case I never figured out how exactly to design the extra card with the rules until I saw how GtG did it. I know I can't post details here but for those that have seen the custom decks on BGG you may have seen some of my stuff. I go by the same name over there too. Even got my main hero drawn by Matthew Bishop&nbsp;(tosx) as thanks for using&nbsp;my templates, which is my current avatar here.</p>",
